@startuml workspace-transfer
' Revision (2026-10-13): accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
' Workspace revision: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); design only.
' Revision: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13); inert review and cumulative obligations; lifetime/performer open.
title R-TRANSFER: dispatcher workspace contract and board exact-candidate path (draft)
participant "Original caller principal" as C
participant "Dispatcher\nno repository; journals digests" as D
database "Dispatcher journal\nplan/digests/export obligation" as J
database "Admitted durable content destination\noutside child home/deletion; storage or handoff unpublished" as S
participant "swarma-workspace-materialize\napproved executor; child UID" as M
participant "Worker\nprivate standalone repository" as W
participant "User manager\naccount-wide stop scope" as H
participant "Project-side executor\nservice principal; workplace fence" as F
participant "swarma-workspace-export\napproved executor; child UID; no network" as X
participant "Board change-request machinery\norchestrator executes; formats unpublished" as B
participant "Admitted review role\ntrusted-class local agent or person holding role\nnot producer; not untrusted" as R
== materialize base B ==
C -> D : admitted base B as bounded canonical tree archive with start
D -> J : archive digest; plan covers immutable B/mode-aware manifest, scope, exec/resources\nexporter digest/caps/repair budget/bounded cleanup consent
D -> M : relay archive; distinct materializer execution claim/launch/receipt
M -> M : verify each archive path/kind/mode/content against immutable B manifest
alt mismatch, missing or extra archive entry
  break no work admission
    M --> D : materialization refusal; no worker delta or candidate
    D -> H : materializer own E-stop/absence; unknown evidence retained
  end
else exact archive-to-manifest match
  M -> W : verified standalone private repository; fresh config; no hooks/remotes/credential helpers
  M -> W : task resources read-only next to workspace; data, never instructions
  D -> H : materializer own E-stop; confirmed account-wide absence before distinct work launch
end
note over D,W
  R-UNTRUSTED: workplace untrusted unless operator act admits remote worker to trusted circle.
  Membership enables donor-side opt-ins only; all host boundaries stay.
  Membership supplies neither review-role nor host-local placement authority (§3.6).
  Every workplace: no subscription binding or host-local loop.
  R-NET-TOOL/R-EXEC: workplace zero egress; protected machine-selected exec body pin.
  Full invocation and interpreted inputs qualified; caller reference is not authority.
  ALLSTOP receiver fence blocks materializer/exporter starts until explicit recovery (§6).
  Worker has no push/merge-request access; code leaves only as platform-taken data.
  R-VERIFY: builds/tests/worker code execution only on off-host secret-free runners.
  Web default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only.
  Worker asks for more resources by letter/outcome and never fetches.
  Manifest derives from immutable B objects, never checkout; encoding/access unpublished.
  Each materialize/work/export launch: own claim, E-launch, receipt, E-stop, absence and round linkage.
  Bounded cleanup consent survives ordinary expiry only; revocation/compromise/holds need explicit recovery.
  No harness/lease/network/repair consent; no exporter after helper retiring or session-permit reuse.
  Accounted bounded cleanup capacity progresses beside forward work; no security/storage exemption.
  Archive/plan/resource/transport/retention formats and cap values unpublished.
  Open requirement (question 31): stage A bridge/helper/dispatcher package must jointly
  reconcile ingress/relay/start/quiesce/export/reconnect and generation-bound creation fence.
  Includes auxiliary UID processes, replacement, watcher/emergency stop and explicit reopening.
  No mechanism/channel lifetime chosen here; existing gates do not claim a qualified lifetime.
  Result schema is DRAFT: schemas/workspace-result-1.schema.json (§5.2.1).
end note
W -> W : edit in admitted write scope; platform ignores worker .git/commits/history
== round end and export ==
W -> C : board outcome (local) or signed final envelope (remote)
C -> D : round end: next round within one work execution; retry keeps round; final is last\nintermediate export at turn boundary; transport/linkage unpublished
D -> J : journal current-execution exec.stop intent; retain export obligation
opt workplace round
  D -> F : close workspace write and SSH account-process ingress fences before quiescence
  F --> D : refuse further tool calls/ingress through export
end
D -> H : exec.stop; account-wide scope
H --> D : confirmed absence of every account process, or unknown/pending
alt absence or required fence unconfirmed
  break no export or candidate
    D -> J : retain claims/obligation; no export or home deletion
    D --> C : pending/unknown evidence
  end
else absence and required fence confirmed
  D -> J : admit exporter under bounded consent/current security evidence; distinct physical launch\nretain same effect for interrupted export; terminal replay never reruns
  D -> X : child-UID export; fixed environment; no network; original launch evidence
  X -> X : no following links; skip .git; compare immutable manifest kind/mode + content\nmode-only/type transitions are modify; deletion uses prior mode; stop at first cap excess
  alt forbidden path/type/collision/submodule/root escape or exceeded cap
    break refused result; no change set or candidate
      X --> D : DRAFT workspace-result/1 refused; reason_class + offending_path; entries empty
      D -> H : exporter own E-stop; confirm absence before any new work launch
      D -> J : immutable terminal refusal/effect/receipt; retain obligation; no C or automatic discard
      D --> C : refused workspace-result/1 under current original-caller authentication; no partial entries/blobs
      opt current work authority + separately admitted repair + plan budget remaining
        C -> D : request bounded fix-up on same workspace; no re-materialization
        D -> F : reopen fences only for admitted repair turn
        D -> W : new linked work execution; class/path only; preserve valid edits
        D -> F : close write/SSH ingress fences again
        D -> H : new work E-stop; account-wide absence before new complete export
        D -> J : count repair against original round budget; new linked export execution/effect\nrepeat full export/custody flow; original refusal stays immutable
      end
      note over D,J : No authority/budget: retain for per-act operator waiver; standing discard off.
      note over C,B : No candidate on refusal; after disposition next ordinary round uses last admitted base.
    end
  else qualified source-entry permission denial
    break typed exporter failure; encoding unpublished; no schema extension
      X --> D : known blocked entry/ancestor; never chmod, ACL mutation or privilege elevation
      D -> H : exporter own E-stop/absence; unknown retains claims
      D -> J : retain terminal failure/obligation; same bounded current-authority repair/per-act waiver disposition
      D --> C : authenticated failure evidence; known blocked entry/ancestor only; no partial change set
      note over D,X : Misapplied sandbox/manifest denial is infrastructure failure, not source refusal.
    end
  else interrupted or unknown export / infrastructure uncertainty
    break no terminal verdict or candidate
      D -> H : reconcile exporter original claim/receipt/E-stop; unknown absence retains claims
      D -> J : pending/unknown; same effect and canonical arguments; resolve original receipt\nEIO/storage/volume/identity uncertainty never discharges obligation
    end
  else valid bounded change set
    X --> D : DRAFT workspace-result/1 recorded; blob SHA-256/size/mode, link text, deletes
    X --> D : content-addressed blobs; no inline file contents (transport unpublished)
    D -> H : exporter own E-stop; confirmed account-wide absence before retirement/next launch
    D -> S : digest/size-verify result and every referenced blob; durable admitted custody
    alt complete-content receipt durable outside deletion
      S --> D : authenticated complete-content receipt (format unpublished)
      D -> J : journal complete-content receipt; discharge obligation; home may retire before import
      D --> C : workspace-result/1 only under current original-caller authentication
    else missing/corrupt blob, storage failure or incomplete receipt
      break retained obligation; no deletion/candidate handoff
        D -> J : pending custody; digest-only journal is insufficient; no truncation
      end
    end
  end
end
== board-owned import and exact-commit review after valid export ==
C -> B : accept result as resource; deterministic import on B
B -> B : independently recompute canonical mode-aware manifest from repository immutable B\nrefuse base_commit != B or manifest_digest mismatch; retain admission checks
B -> B : scratch index; no hooks/attribute filters/drivers
B -> B : refuse .git, outside write scope, .task-board; flag sensitive paths and every symlink
B -> B : sign candidate C with repository identity; worker/run/result-digest trailers
B -> B : verify C tree equals recomputed B plus change set
B -> D : authenticated import acknowledgement (format unpublished)
D -> S : release retained content only on authenticated acknowledgement or other explicit authorized release
B -> B : recompute full candidate delta/sensitive-hunk set against trusted integration baseline\nnot rework base B or verification H; include inherited sensitive changes/symlinks\nsurface unresolved inherited provenance separately from current-run capability class
B -> R : exact-C inert diffs/blobs; read-only by digest outside discovery roots\npositive role/class/placement admission; execution only in R-VERIFY
note over B,R
  Candidate files are data, never automatically adopted as control surfaces.
  Covers startup/reload/nested discovery/resume/child entry before or after acknowledgement.
  Discovery-capable tree entry requires qualified strict-context adapter; root surfaces alone insufficient.
  Acknowledgement records no preceding automatic load; inert path satisfies ordering by construction.
  Verdict does not admit instructions/hooks/MCP/permissions/skills; separate control-context decision.
  Semantic prompt injection remains a review risk; optional reviewer policies off/unchosen.
end note
R --> B : fresh verdict bound to exact C (K1), integration baseline and complete flagged set\nexplicit hunk acknowledgements; inherited provenance resolution is exact-candidate bound
alt changes requested
  B -> C : findings; next admitted base C
  C -> D : next round archive from C; remote signed letter or local task snapshot
  D -> M : verify/materialize fresh workspace from immutable C manifest\nold home removal only after complete-content custody or per-act waiver
  M -> W : rework on C; donor-side session continues for remote worker
  W -> W : next fenced round/export produces C2 on C; repeat exact-candidate review
  note over B,R
    Recompute against same trusted integration baseline; retain inherited sensitive/provenance obligations.
    Fresh exact-C2 acknowledgements/verdict; no carry-over; fully reverted sensitive changes drop out.
    Baseline refresh requires re-review; rewording alone cannot clear provenance.
    Clearance needs published conservative removal/provenance rule or exact-candidate resolution.
    Current-run capability class stays factual; acknowledgement does not complete provenance.
  end note
else exact C accepted
  B -> B : signed fast-forward of accepted exact head (K1/K3)
  note right of B : Moved base requires ordinary refresh and re-review.
  note over C,B
    Open requirement (question 32): stage T board/infrastructure package must name non-agent
    external-effect performer, request/result paths, custody/routes and per-effect validation.
    Covers pending publication, verification handoff, base refresh and exact-head landing.
    Topology remains owner/infrastructure choice; no agent credential/egress or new service selected.
  end note
end
note over D,J
  Four classes: recorded export, deterministic refusal, interrupted/unknown, per-act authorized discard.
  Qualified source permission failure uses the same repair/waiver disposition; format unpublished.
  Refused effect immutable; same-tree class/recorded-delta conflict contradictory, diagnostics may vary.
  Retain complete content outside deletion until authenticated import acknowledgement/authorized release.
  Unavailable caller consumes bounded retained storage; silent pre-import expiry is not delivery.
  Export custody precedes helper retiring/home deletion; only per-act operator waiver discards.
  Refusal retains live allocation/home/UID, not work execution slot after confirmed absence.
  No relaxed home permissions or recursive chown; dispatcher holds no repository.
  Import/candidate/review/integration belong to the board and remain unpublished here.
  Remote-workplace protocol v2.1 sections 8 and 10 gates adopted; executor exports under UID.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: §§3.6, 4.2, 5.2-5.4, 14, 16 question 22.
  workspace-result/1 fields and closed reason classes are explicitly authorized DRAFT (§5.2.1).
  Other design labels do not publish commands, wire fields, refusal codes or cap values.
  Round-end and blob transport remain unpublished (§16 question 22).
endlegend
@enduml
